{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>This is the day that YHWH has made</b> — זאת referring to that which is wondrous in our eyes — like (1 Samuel 14:6) עשה ה' לנו 'perhaps YHWH will do for us' ככל נפלאותיו 'like all His wonders.' And Rabbi Moses said: for the verbs stand in place of noun-forms, as though it said, 'This is the day YHWH made for gladness and joy in it' — and like it (1 Samuel 2:3): אל תרבו תדברו 'do not multiply speaking' (i.e., the verbs function as verbal nouns). And in my opinion: all of them are missing a shin [prefix], and so they are שנגילה ונשמחה בו, אל תרבו שתדברו, ונדעה שנרדפה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra argues that the verbs in his proof-texts lack an expected ש prefix (short for אשר, 'that/which'); he restores it in each case."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:06.948337972Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}